cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PGAA, please cite this software repository."
title: "PGAA: a claim-state compiler for perturbation-transcriptomic evidence"
type: software
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/xutaoguo55/pgaa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xutaoguo55/pgaa"
abstract: "PGAA is an executable claim-state compiler for perturbation transcriptomics, provided as a Python and R package. It combines internal decision state, ranking stability, external evidence, source-data provenance, and branch-specific promotion gates to emit bounded manuscript claim states, so that an exploratory signal cannot be promoted to a biological or translational conclusion without the evidence a promotion rule requires. Distribution-aware Wasserstein and histogram-shape statistics remain available as upstream scoring modules; they are not claimed as the main methodological novelty."
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - Perturb-seq
  - claim state
  - reproducibility
  - evidence gating
  - CRISPR screening
